    "question": {
        "name": "CSEC Phy May 2022 Q6b — Battery Charging Chain",
        "text": "<p>A battery charger is used to charge a battery. The charger delivers a current of <strong>0.8 A</strong> to the battery.</p><ul><li>Total charge stored: <strong>Q = 9 600 C</strong></li><li>Power input of charger: <strong>P = 4.4 W</strong></li></ul>",
        "general_feedback": "<p><strong>(i) Time to charge:</strong> Q = It → t = Q/I = 9 600 / 0.8 = <strong>12 000 s</strong></p><p><strong>(ii) Voltage:</strong> P = VI → V = P/I = 4.4 / 0.8 = <strong>5.5 V</strong></p><p><strong>(iii) Work done:</strong> W = QV = 9 600 × 5.5 = <strong>52 800 J</strong></p><p><em>Alternative for (iii):</em> W = Pt = 4.4 × 12 000 = 52 800 J ✓</p>"
    },
